Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Diagnostic Performance vs Latent Dimension", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9868849*^9, 
  3.9868849*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"e2e84ab4-c5f1-4e7d-98a4-513f5c7f7c43"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Parameters regression", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.986887723884878*^9, 
  3.986887738564056*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"a232e366-7576-4426-aaf2-\
e666a909e918"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook summarizes diagonal-test performance for ENCA models trained \
with different latent-space dimensions. For each z dimension, the diagnostic \
output provides the Pearson correlation and normalized RMSE for each physical \
parameter. The plots compare correlation with a baseline-corrected \
performance score, using the prior-mean predictor as the zero-performance \
reference.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9868849*^9, 3.9868849*^9}},
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.75, 0, 0.33],ExpressionUUID->"02c1f2b1-70d7-4d1e-a6d8-6d29e1ed9f94"],

Cell["\<\
The numerical pairs below are copied from the output of diag_test.py. For \
each parameter and latent dimension, the first number is the Pearson \
correlation between true and predicted parameter values, and the second \
number is RMSE divided by the prior range, reported in percent.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9868852*^9, 3.9868852*^9}},
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.75, 0, 0.33],ExpressionUUID->"49bfe3ad-0f14-4d7e-a58b-bc9a7d901f89"],

